are normal fleshy material] gives one method this might be acheived,
if you want to read a good and rather silly mystery novel.) At any
rate, it was meant as just one way you could explain the
random-but-rare instant death of a wood golem when struck by an axe.

Alternatively, how about an artifact axe that had (as above) no
instant kill rate against most creatures, but a much higher one
against wood golems- say, 25-50%- and that could be used as a more
efficient means than kicking to break down doors? I'd rate the
usefulness of such a thing right up there with good old Sting and
